  </tbody>
</table>

<p>For a side hustle, Basic is the right plan until you are doing serious volume. The jump to Grow saves you 0.2 percentage points on card fees, which only pays for the extra $66 a month once you are processing well over $30,000 a month online. The third-party gateway fee only applies if you use a processor other than Shopify Payments, so most new sellers should just turn Shopify Payments on and avoid it.</p>

<div class="callout callout-warn"><strong>Watch out:</strong> Apps are where Shopify costs creep. Reviews, upsells, email and subscription apps often run $5–$30 a month each. Start with the free tier of anything you install and add paid apps only when they earn their keep.</div>

<h2 id="business-models">Five Shopify business models that fit a side hustle</h2>
<p>Pick a model before you pick a product. The model decides your margin, your workload and how much cash you put at risk.</p>

<div class="hustle-grid">
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="print-on-demand">Print-on-demand</h3>
    <p>You design shirts, mugs, posters or phone cases; a supplier like Printful or Printify prints and ships each order after it is paid. No inventory, but base costs are high, so your design and niche have to justify a premium price.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Startup:</b> Under $100</li><li><b>Margin:</b> Thin unless the niche is specific</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Designers, niche communities</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="dropshipping">Dropshipping</h3>
    <p>You list products a supplier ships directly to customers. Easy to start and brutally competitive. Winning stores usually add something: faster US shipping, bundles, better photos or a tight niche.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Startup:</b> $100–$500 (mostly ad tests)</li><li><b>Margin:</b> Squeezed by ad costs</li><li><b>Best for:</b> People who like paid ads</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="digital-products">Digital products</h3>
    <p>Templates, presets, printables, planners, sewing patterns, guides. Near-100% gross margin and instant delivery through a free digital downloads app. Pairs well with an audience you build on social or YouTube.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Startup:</b> Almost nothing</li><li><b>Margin:</b> The highest of any model</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Creators, teachers, designers</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="handmade">Handmade goods</h3>
    <p>Candles, jewelry, soap, custom shirts, woodwork. Your own store keeps more per sale than a marketplace and lets you build an email list, though many makers keep Etsy running alongside it for discovery.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Startup:</b> Materials plus tools</li><li><b>Margin:</b> Strong if you price your time</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Makers with a repeatable product</li></ul>
  </div>
  <div class="hustle-card">
    <h3 id="local-pickup">Local pickup and delivery</h3>
    <p>Baked goods (check your state's cottage food rules), meal prep, plants, refurbished furniture. Shopify supports local pickup and local delivery zones, which cuts out shipping costs entirely.</p>
    <ul class="meta"><li><b>Startup:</b> Low</li><li><b>Margin:</b> Good, no shipping eats it</li><li><b>Best for:</b> Neighborhood and city sellers</li></ul>
  </div>
</div>

<h2 id="margins">Realistic margins: do the math before you launch</h2>
<p>Most failed stores did not fail on product; they failed on unit economics. Here is a simple example for a $30 product shipped to the customer:</p>

<table class="data">
  <thead><tr><th>Line item</th><th>Amount</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Sale price</td><td>$30.00</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Product or print cost</td><td>−$12.00</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Shipping you pay</td><td>−$5.00</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Shopify Payments (2.9% + 30¢)</td><td>−$1.17</td></tr>
    <tr><td><strong>Profit before marketing</strong></td><td><strong>$11.83</strong></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>If it costs you $8 in ads to win that order, you keep under $4. That is why the healthiest side hustle stores raise average order value (bundles, free-shipping thresholds) and lean on free traffic: Pinterest, short-form video, search and email. Plug your own numbers into the calculator below to find your break-even ad spend.</p>

[[tool:shopify-profit]]

