<h2 id="shopify-adjacent">Shopify side hustles that do not need a store</h2>
<p>Millions of merchants run on Shopify, and many would rather pay someone than learn it. If you like the platform more than the idea of selling products, these are often faster paths to income.</p>

<h3 id="store-setup">Store setup freelancing</h3>
<p>Small businesses pay freelancers to build a store from a theme: products imported, payments configured, policies written, apps installed. Package it as a fixed-price offer ("5-page store, 20 products, launched in 7 days") and sell it on <a href="/fiverr/">Fiverr</a> or directly to local businesses. Use the <a href="/tools/freelance-rate-calculator/">freelance rate calculator</a> to price packages so you are not working for minimum wage after platform fees.</p>

<h3 id="theme-customization">Theme customization and speed fixes</h3>
<p>If you know some HTML, CSS and Shopify's Liquid templating language, merchants pay for custom sections, design tweaks and page speed improvements. Joining the free Shopify Partner Program gives you development stores to build and test in, and listings in Shopify's partner directory once you qualify.</p>

<h3 id="shopify-collabs">Shopify Collabs for creators</h3>
<p>Shopify Collabs is Shopify's free app that connects merchants with creators. Brands set commission rates and send affiliate links, discount codes or free product; you post, and commissions are paid automatically. If you already make content on Instagram, TikTok or YouTube, it is a way to earn from Shopify brands without any inventory. Eligibility rules (follower counts, countries) can change, so check the current requirements when you apply.</p>

<h3 id="shopify-affiliate">The Shopify Affiliate Program</h3>
<p>If you write or make videos about starting a business, the <a href="https://www.shopify.com/affiliates">Shopify Affiliate Program</a> pays up to $150 per qualified referral, with amounts varying by the referral's country, as of 2026. It runs on Impact, tracks clicks for 30 days, and credits free-trial signups for up to 400 days if they move to a paid, full-price plan. There is a $10 minimum withdrawal and applications are reviewed, so you need an active site or channel first. Estimate what your traffic could earn with the <a href="/tools/affiliate-commission-calculator/">affiliate commission calculator</a>.</p>

<h2 id="get-traffic">How to get your first 100 customers</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Search:</strong> Write helpful collection and blog pages around what your buyers type into Google. Keyword research tools like <a href="/semrush/">Semrush</a> show you which terms have volume and weak competition.</li>
  <li><strong>Short-form video:</strong> Show the product in use, the packing process or the making-of. This works especially well for handmade and print-on-demand.</li>
  <li><strong>Pinterest:</strong> Still one of the best free traffic sources for home goods, printables and gifts.</li>
  <li><strong>Email:</strong> Offer a small first-order discount for signups. Your list is the one channel no algorithm can take away.</li>
  <li><strong>Local:</strong> Farmers markets, pop-ups and community groups for local pickup stores.</li>
</ul>
<p>If marketing is the part you enjoy, it can become its own income stream; see our <a href="/digital-marketing-side-hustle/">digital marketing side hustle</a> guide.</p>

<h2 id="taxes">Taxes and bookkeeping</h2>
<p>Store profit is self-employment income. Set aside money for federal income tax plus self-employment tax, track every expense (plan fees, apps, samples, shipping supplies, ads), and collect sales tax where required. The <a href="/tools/self-employment-tax-calculator/">self-employment tax calculator</a> shows how much to set aside each month. Keep a separate bank account for the store from day one; it makes tax season dramatically easier.</p>

<h2 id="mistakes">Mistakes that sink new Shopify stores</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Building for weeks before testing demand.</strong> A store with three products and real traffic teaches you more than a polished store nobody visits. Launch ugly, then improve what customers actually click.</li>
  <li><strong>Pricing from cost instead of from value.</strong> Doubling your cost often is not enough once shipping, payment fees, returns and ads come out. Price against what similar products sell for, then check the math with the calculator above.</li>
  <li><strong>Copying a viral dropshipping product.</strong> By the time a product is trending in "winning product" videos, hundreds of stores are bidding on the same ads. Look for products with steady, boring demand instead.</li>
  <li><strong>Ignoring shipping times.</strong> Buyers expect delivery in days, not weeks. If your supplier ships slowly from overseas, say so clearly on the product page, or find a supplier with US warehouses.</li>
  <li><strong>Installing every app.</strong> Each app adds monthly cost and can slow your pages. Slow pages lose sales, especially on phones.</li>
  <li><strong>Quitting at month two.</strong> Most stores need several rounds of product, price and creative testing. Decide up front how much time and money you will invest before you judge the result, then stick to that budget.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="time-commitment">How much time it takes</h2>
<p>Expect 15–25 hours to launch a basic store if you are new to Shopify, most of it spent on product photos, descriptions and settings. After launch, a print-on-demand or digital store can run on 5–10 hours a week, almost all of it marketing. Handmade and local stores take more because you are also producing and fulfilling orders. Block that time on your calendar like a shift; stores that get attention only when you feel like it rarely grow.</p>

<h2 id="bottom-line">The bottom line</h2>
<p>A Shopify side hustle rewards people who treat it like a small business: pick a model with real margin, launch lean, and spend most of your time on getting traffic rather than tweaking the theme. If you would rather earn from the platform without the inventory or ad risk, store setup gigs, Collabs and the affiliate program are legitimate alternatives. Not sure which path fits you? Take the Better Side Hustles <a href="/tools/side-hustle-quiz/">side hustle quiz</a>.</p>
